From d3b5ba2c30380c18cd26bb2a974929f743b0479a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xiaowang <quic_xiaowang@quicinc.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Oct 2022 15:15:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] BT Snoop: Add profilesfiltered advance snoop property

- Add profilesfiltered advance bt snoop logs property
- Enabled for all builds including eng/userdebug
CRs-Fixed: 3311851

BT Snoop: Add Advnace snoop properties (3/4)

Add Advance snoop property
CRs-Fixed: 3264880

BT snoop: Add snooplog filter for specfic profiles

Profiles to be supported: pbap, map
Also support +CPBR response filtering for HFP if pbap profile is enabled.
Works only in user build
There are 3 filter modes:
fullfilter - Discard whole packet
header     - Keep ACL&L2CAP header
magic      - Keep ACL&L2CAP header and fill magic string
Configuration properies:
persist.bluetooth.btsnooplogmode = profilesfiltered
persist.bluetooth.snoopfilter.profiles = pbap/map
persist.bluetooth.snoopfilter.mode = fullfilter/header/magic
CRs-Fixed: 2842095

Add Filtering for vendor snoop logs (1/4)

 - Added new filtering options Enabled Headers Filtered
   and Enabled Media Pkts Filtered in snoop logging.
 - Added logic to capture vendor snoop logs and filtered
   vendor snoop logs enabled from developer options
CRs-Fixed: 2426675

Add Filtering for snoop logs based on L2CAP and RFCOMM Channels (1/4)

* Change btsnoop logging into disabled, filtered, and full modes
* When ro.isdebuggable is 1, filtered logging is enabled by default
* Otherwise, disabled by default
* When legacy mode is enabled, translate it to full and reset legacy
  property to empty
Bug: 112970672
Bug: 67669544
Test: See that the snoop file always exists but is filtered when
snooplogs are disabled and unfiltered when enabled.
(cherry picked from commit 9eafd0989d32a95b6a83396cc9cb9e7b91cbfaa1)

BT: Modified logging framework for unified logging

- A new process is introduced for BT logging to
  capture all logs with log level 6.
- Changes made in existing logging framework to
  send all logs to new BT logger process
  irrespective of logging level of each module.
- Logs will be captured from BT ON to OFF.
- Logger process is started on as part stack init
  and stopped on cleanup.
-  Fix for occasional blockage while snoop
   module shut down
- Socket activity while snoop module shutdown
  causes it to block leading to disable timeout.
- Made changes to shutdown the socket before
  closing the thread.
CRs-Fixed: 2130741
Change-Id: Ic4caf1d1b1d7c3723697b02f52fd48f0dbb76249
BLUETOOTH: Add feature to control logging level
-> These changes are framework to control the level
   of logging that will be done by bt_logger
-> User can set a property to enable/disable one or
   more logging functionalities.
-> Added option to filter out media packets from
   hci snoop logs.
CRs-Fixed: 2133811
